step Additional Runecloth to Honored
  zone Darnassus
  tip Additional Runecloth: 50 reputation for 20 Runecloth, as often as you like. After the four first donations a Human, Dwarf or Gnome stands at Friendly 700 of 6,000, so Honored is 5,300 away: 106 turn-ins, 2,120 Runecloth (Night Elves start 900 higher: 88 turn-ins; Skyborne start at Neutral 500, so 7,900 away: 158, two fewer after Exploring the Alliance). The True Masters and the Morrowgrain chain above take 8 turn-ins off, and every 10 Morrowgrain you hand in counts as one more; each hub you did takes 20 to 28 more off if it paid in full. More quests pay Darnassus, in full while they are no more than 5 levels below you: the rest of Darkshore (about 3,400 more), Astranaar in Ashenvale (about 3,900) and Feathermoon in Feralas (about 1,700). Every city gain also gives a quarter as much to the other three Alliance cities (not counted here). Hand in all your Runecloth at once.
  collect 14047 x20 optional nearest
  turnin 7801 direct optional
  rep 69 Honored

step Additional Runecloth to Revered
  tip Honored: in Classic Darnassus's vendors take 10% off for you, Lelanai's nightsabers (20g, the swift ones 200g) included; Forever has not settled it, and guide sites report 5% at Friendly rising to 20% at Exalted. Honored to Revered is 12,000 reputation: 240 turn-ins, 4,800 Runecloth.
  collect 14047 x20 optional nearest
  turnin 7801 direct optional
  rep 69 Revered

step Additional Runecloth to Exalted
  tip Revered to Exalted is 21,000 reputation: 420 turn-ins, 8,400 Runecloth. At Exalted, Lelanai at the Cenarion Enclave in Darnassus sells her nightsabers to other races in Classic; the Saber and Swift Saber guides cover them.
  collect 14047 x20 optional nearest
  turnin 7801 direct optional
  rep 69 Exalted
